<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kallanai Dam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Grand Anicut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kallanai, or Grand Anicut, is an ancient dam across the Kaveri River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Tamil tradition credits its construction to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> king Karikala in the early centuries CE, making it one of the oldest water-diversion works still in use. It was rebuilt and enlarged by British engineers in the 19th century and still feeds the irrigation of the Kaveri delta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kallanai-dam.jpg" alt="Kallanai Dam" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ashwin Kumar from Bangalore, India · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Anicut,_Kallanai_(11876067114).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
